  "verbalization": "Nudifloside B appears to be a potential inhibitor of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, as it targets the CD276 antigen, which is a known target of multiple compounds, including Taiwanin E Methyl Ether, 2,4-Dibromo-6-(3,4,6-Tribromo-2-Methoxyphenoxy)Phenol, and 6-O-Veratroylcatalpol. These compounds all share a common mechanism of action, targeting the CD276 antigen and subsequently influencing the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The scores from the three paths suggest a consistent and plausible relationship, with Nudifloside B acting as a mediator in this pathway. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Nudifloside B and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and the specific mode of action. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same antigen reinforces the likelihood of a shared biological pathway, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
